Verified layout (compiled on host):
- `sizeof(superblock_t)=512`, `sizeof(inode_t)=64`, `sizeof(dir_entry_t)=32`, `sizeof(dir_t)=4096`, `sizeof(fd_t)=24`.
- `dir_entry_t` offsets: `type=0`, `name=1` (29 bytes → names up to 28 chars + NUL), **`inode=30`** (2 pad-free bytes at 30..31).
- `inode_t` offsets: `mode=0`, `owner=4`, `size=8`, `direct_blocks=12`, `indirect_blocks=52`, `link=60`.
- `fd_t` offsets: `inode=0`, `access=2`, `rd_pos=8`, `wr_pos=16`.

Cache-region sizes implied by the `*_CACHE` constants:
| region | kva | bytes | sectors |
|---|---|---|---|
| superblock | `0xffffffc05f000000` | 0x200 = 512 | 1 |
| inode map | `0xffffffc05f000200` | 0x200 = 512 | 1 |
| block map | `0xffffffc05f000400` | 0x8000 = 32768 | 64 |
| inode (one sector = 8 inodes) | `0xffffffc05f008400` | 0x200 = 512 | 1 |
| block (one 4 KB block) | `0xffffffc05f008600` | 0x1000 = 4096 | 8 |
| end | `0xffffffc05f009600` | — | — |

These kvas are backed: `include/os/mm.h:42` documents `0x5f00_0000 ~ 0x6000_0000  FS Cache`, `PGDIR_END 0x5f000000`, `MEM_END 0x60000000`; `arch/riscv/kernel/boot.c:map_kernel_page()` maps 128 × 2 MB from pa `0x50000000` (256 MB) at both identity and `KERNEL_MEM_OFFSET`, so pa `0x5f000000` is mapped RWX.

There is only **one** inode-sector cache and **one** block cache — nested lookups must re-read.

