Only `include/os/mm.h` differs (P6 carves `PGDIR_END 0x5f000000` out for an FS cache). So P6's `net.c` can be transplanted verbatim into P5.

Also note: this is **not** an e1000/"GigabitEthernet" register set. It is the **Xilinx Zynq PS GEM (EMACPS / Cadence macb)** driver. There is **no** `mac_send_desc`, `mac_recv_desc`, `set_sram_ctrl`, or `net_poll_mode()` function anywhere in the tree (`grep -rn "mac_send_desc\|mac_recv_desc\|set_sram_ctrl\|GigabitEthernet\|e1000"` → 0 hits). `net_poll_mode` is an **int global**, not a function.

