```c
int do_mkfs(int mode, int* print_location_y)
{
    read_superblock();
    if(mode == 1){ superblock->magic = 0x0; write_superblock(); }
    if(superblock->magic == MAGIC){ return 0; }
    mkfs(1);
    enable_sum();
    *print_location_y = *print_location_y + 11;   // mkfs(1) must print exactly 11 lines
    disable_sum();
    return 1;
}

void do_statfs(int* print_location_y)
{
    read_superblock();
    prints("used inode: %d/%d\n", superblock->used_inode_num, superblock->inode_num);
    prints("used block: %d/%d\n", superblock->used_block_num, superblock->block_num);
    enable_sum();
    *print_location_y = *print_location_y + 2;
    disable_sum();
}
```
Globals defined in fs.c: `superblock`(=`SUPERBLOCK_CACHE`), `blockmap`, `inodemap`, `cached_inode_base`, `cached_block_base`, `cached_inode_id`, `cached_block_id`, `current_dir_inode`, `current_dir_block`.

Hard contracts implied by the pre-written code: `mkfs(1)` prints exactly **11** lines and `mkfs(0)` must print none; `mkfs()` returns non-zero iff it actually formatted (main.c prints "Initialized Successfully" vs "No Need to Initialize"); `superblock->{used_inode_num,inode_num,used_block_num,block_num}` must be maintained; `do_mkfs` never re-reads the superblock after `mkfs()`, so `mkfs()` must leave `SUPERBLOCK_CACHE` coherent.

### FS constants you must obey (`include/os/fs.h`, `include/os/disk.h`, `include/os/file.h`)
```c
#define MAGIC            0x200006042018fffflu
#define SUPERBLOCK_CACHE 0xffffffc05f000000lu   // 512 B
#define INODEMAP_CACHE   0xffffffc05f000200lu   // 512 B  (1 sector = 4096 inodes)
#define BLOCKMAP_CACHE   0xffffffc05f000400lu   // 32 KiB (64 sectors = 262144 blocks)
#define INODE_CACHE      0xffffffc05f008400lu   // 512 B  (8 inodes/sector)
#define BLOCK_CACHE      0xffffffc05f008600lu   // 4 KiB
#define FS_CACHE_END     0xffffffc05f009600lu
// superblock_t: 15 x uint64_t + uint8_t empty[392] == 512 B
// inode_t (64 B): mode, owner, size, direct_blocks[10], indirect_blocks[2], link (all u32)
// dir_entry_t (32 B): uint8_t type; uint8_t name[29]; uint16_t inode;  EMPTY=0 DIR=1 FILE=2
// dir_t: dir_entry_t entry[128]  == 4096 B
#define SUPERBLOCK_ID     4096
#define BLOCKMAP_BEGIN_ID 4097   // 64 sectors
#define INODEMAP_ID       4161
#define INODE_BEGIN_ID    4162   // 512 sectors -> 4096 inodes
#define BLOCK_BEGIN_ID    5120   // 8 sectors per 4 KiB block
// fd_t: uint16_t inode; uint16_t access; uint64_t rd_pos; uint64_t wr_pos;  fd_list[10]
// O_EMPTY 0, O_RDONLY 1, O_WRONLY 2, O_RDWR 3
```
SBI transport: `sbi_sd_read/write(unsigned int mem_address /*PA*/, unsigned int num_of_blocks, unsigned int block_id)` = ecall #11 / #10 (`arch/riscv/include/asm/sbidef.h`). Note the args are `unsigned int`, so you must pass `kva2pa(...)`, as `disk.c` already does.

