**`kernel/mm/mm.c`: NO — byte-for-byte identical.** Both md5 `30b88811122e75fc6a7fafbc54b1407e`. Same 9 stubs at the same line numbers, same includes, same globals, same implemented helpers. Note that the *behaviour* still changes because `include/os/mm.h` shrinks `PGDIR_PAGE_NUM` (8189 → 4093 pages), which changes `pgdir_page[]`'s size and the `assert(i != PGDIR_PAGE_NUM)` bound inside `alloc_pgdir_page()`.

